  "notes": "TRUE catalog program name: 'Academic Plan for Bachelor of Science/Arts, AREA: COMPUTER SCIENCE', Department of Computer Science and Information Systems, Murray State University. Source: official Murray State document 'Academic-Plan-for-BABS-CSC.pdf' (2 pages, marked 'May 11, 2021'), downloaded live from the CSIS department's official site (source_url above) on 2026-09-30. CATALOG-YEAR HONESTY: this is the 2020-2021 catalog edition - the department's only published full freshman-to-senior term-by-term sequence for the general Computer Science program; it is STALE (5 years old). The current catalog is Kuali-hosted and was not reachable from this environment, but the core major course set in this plan (CSC 100T/101/145/300/325/345/405/410/415/425/430/445/455/530/540, CSC 232-or-233-or-235, CIS 407, CNM 135) matches the current catalog's published BA/BS Computer Science program requirements. Transcription method: read the official PDF and transcribed course-by-course; per-term subtotals cross-checked against the plan's layout (15+15+15+15+15+15+15+15=120). Degree total: 120 credits (University Studies 41 + Area 52 + free electives 27). The source document covers both the BA and BS; this plan is filed as the BS. Note: the source says students pursuing the BA in CSC must complete 12 hours of a foreign language, which reduces the free electives shown here. Title sourcing: most course titles verified against the official Murray State 2018-19 bulletin course descriptions (murraystate.edu). Three titles are NOT in the 2018-19 bulletin (courses added later): CSC 455 'Computer Security', CNM 135 'Introduction to Cybersecurity and Network Management', and CSC 425 'Web-Based Services and Applications' (the 2018-19 bulletin titled CSC 425 'Mobile and Web Programming'; the newer title is the one used in Murray State's current published program requirements and transfer records) - all three titles flagged as post-2018-19. Placement note from the source: STA 135 requires college-level math readiness - 'take prerequisite MAT class in place of STA 135 if necessary'; MAT 250 requires MAT 140 & 145 (or MAT 150) if the math ACT score is below 26. Prereq arrays are left empty because the source document explicitly defers prerequisites to the Bulletin ('See Bulletin for course prerequisites and course sequencing').",
